= January 2020 — The first opposition succession

At the campaign opening, **Grzegorz Schetyna** still led Civic Platform. He
had rebuilt KO as a broad alliance, but two national defeats and the loss of
government made his control the issue in a direct membership ballot. Schetyna
stood aside and backed Tomasz Siemoniak; members instead gave **Borys Budka** a
first-round mandate.

**Outgoing → incoming:** Grzegorz Schetyna → Borys Budka.  
**Incoming bloc:** [+ ko_incoming_bloc +].  
**Why now:** members want a more visible parliamentary opposition and a reset
before the presidential election, without dismantling KO's alliance.

For Lewica, a younger chair may cooperate on constitutional defence while
competing harder for urban, professional and anti-PiS voters. The response
must therefore define a relationship, not pretend the new leader is a Left
appointment.

- @budka_social
- @budka_democratic
- @budka_compete

@budka_social
title: Offer Budka a joint social-opposition working group
